From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:25:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Initialise the auto-CMD12 argument on the A733

When a multiple-block transfer is sent without CMD23, the controller
ends it with a CMD12 of its own and takes the argument from SMHC_A12A.
On the A733 that register resets to 0x0000ffff, and the driver has
never written it, so the automatic stop goes out with 0xffff instead of
the zero argument CMD12 takes. On eMMC 4.41 and later, bit 0 of that
argument selects the high priority interrupt form of the command.

Write zero to SMHC_A12A in sunxi_mmc_init_host(), which runs after
every controller reset, behind a new configuration flag set only for
the A733. The flag keeps the other controllers as they are: their
reset values have not been checked here.

The value only matters for transfers without CMD23. On the A733 those
are the ones whose card does not support CMD23, since the controller
sends CMD23 by itself otherwise.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; SMHC_A12A reads 0 on
the SD and the eMMC controller, also after a runtime suspend and resume.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index 9a2850710152..731f5d3ad275 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -316,6 +316,9 @@ struct sunxi_mmc_cfg {
 	/* controller has the HS400 data strobe path, and its initial delay */
 	bool can_hs400;
 	u32 ds_dl;
+
+	/* SMHC_A12A does not reset to zero, the auto-CMD12 argument */
+	bool needs_a12a_init;
 };
 
 struct sunxi_mmc_host {
@@ -398,6 +401,9 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_init_host(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host)
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_RINTR, 0xffffffff);
 	/* Debug register? undocumented */
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_DBGC, 0xdeb);
+	/* Argument of the CMD12 the controller sends by itself */
+	if (host->cfg->needs_a12a_init)
+		mmc_writel(host, REG_A12A, 0);
 	/* Enable CEATA support */
 	if (!host->cfg->no_ceata_funs)
 		mmc_writel(host, REG_FUNS, SDXC_CEATA_ON);
@@ -1444,6 +1450,7 @@ static const struct sunxi_mmc_cfg sun60i_a733_cfg = {
 	.thld_fifo_bytes = 1024,
 	.can_hs400 = true,
 	.ds_dl = 20,
+	.needs_a12a_init = true,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id sunxi_mmc_of_match[] = {
